<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

	<!--
		velocity-engine-core shades (embeds) an older commons-io inside its JAR.
		CVE-2024-47554 is a DoS vulnerability in commons-io's XmlStreamReader, which
		Velocity does not use. Velocity is pulled transitively by the SAML stack
		(spring-security-saml2-service-provider -> net.shibboleth:shib-velocity:9.2.2 ->
		velocity-engine-core), not by solr-solrj; EntryStore does not use Velocity at all.
		The shaded commons-io cannot be overridden without upgrading Velocity itself, which
		is controlled by the OpenSAML/Shibboleth dependency.
	-->
	<!-- Added 2026-04-01. Re-evaluate when the OpenSAML/Shibboleth SAML stack drops or upgrades velocity-engine-core. -->
	<suppress>
		<notes><![CDATA[
			CVE-2024-47554: DoS in commons-io XmlStreamReader, shaded inside velocity-engine-core
			(transitive from the SAML stack: spring-security-saml2-service-provider -> shib-velocity ->
			velocity-engine-core, not solr-solrj). Velocity does not exercise the vulnerable code path
			and EntryStore does not use Velocity. The shaded commons-io cannot be overridden without
			upgrading Velocity, which is controlled by the OpenSAML/Shibboleth dependency.
		]]></notes>
		<filePath regex="true">.*velocity-engine-core.*</filePath>
		<cve>CVE-2024-47554</cve>
	</suppress>

	<!--
		CVE-2026-54515 / GHSA-5jmj-h7xm-6q6v: case-insensitive deserialization
		(@JsonFormat ACCEPT_CASE_INSENSITIVE_PROPERTIES) bypasses per-property @JsonIgnoreProperties
		in jackson-databind. No fixed Jackson 2.x release exists yet: 2.21.x ends at 2.21.4 and 2.18.x
		at 2.18.8, the announced 2.21.5 / 2.18.9 are unpublished, and 2.22.0 (latest) is also affected.
		Only Jackson 3.x is patched (3.1.4), which EntryStore already uses for its own (de)serialization.
		The flagged jackson-databind 2.x is transitive-only (solr-solrj, rdf4j-rio-api); EntryStore never
		deserializes untrusted input through it. Integrity-only, CVSS 5.3.
	-->
	<!-- Added 2026-07-01. Remove and bump Jackson 2.x to 2.21.5 once it is released (ENTRYSTORE-1068). -->
	<suppress>
		<notes><![CDATA[
			CVE-2026-54515 / GHSA-5jmj-h7xm-6q6v in transitive jackson-databind 2.x (via solr-solrj,
			rdf4j-rio-api). No patched 2.x release exists yet; EntryStore's own code is on Jackson 3
			(3.1.4, fixed) and never deserializes untrusted input via Jackson 2. Bump to 2.21.5 when released.
		]]></notes>
		<packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.fasterxml\.jackson\.core/jackson-databind@.*$</packageUrl>
		<cve>CVE-2026-54515</cve>
		<vulnerabilityName>GHSA-5jmj-h7xm-6q6v</vulnerabilityName>
	</suppress>

	<!--
		CVE-2026-44825: hardcoded default credentials installed by the Apache Solr SERVER's
		"bin/solr auth enable" setup tool. EntryStore embeds the SolrJ CLIENT (solr-solrj /
		solr-solrj-jetty) to reach an externally-run Solr; the client jar does not contain bin/solr and
		EntryStore never runs that tool. dependency-check matched purely on the apache:solr version CPE.
		False positive.
	-->
	<!-- Added 2026-07-01. -->
	<suppress>
		<notes><![CDATA[
			CVE-2026-44825 is in the Solr server "bin/solr auth enable" setup tool, not the SolrJ client
			library. EntryStore embeds solr-solrj to reach an external Solr and never runs that tool.
			CPE version-only match; false positive.
		]]></notes>
		<packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.solr/solr-solrj(-jetty)?@.*$</packageUrl>
		<cve>CVE-2026-44825</cve>
	</suppress>

	<!--
		CVE-2026-53914: unsafe deserialization in Kotlin's build-cache metadata (compile-time / Kotlin
		build tooling). EntryStore is a Java project; kotlin-stdlib is only a runtime transitive (RDF4J
		LMDB / native sails) and never exercises the build-cache code path. Not reachable at runtime.
	-->
	<!-- Added 2026-07-01. Optional: bump kotlin.version to >= 2.4.20 to clear the scanner match. -->
	<suppress>
		<notes><![CDATA[
			CVE-2026-53914 is unsafe deserialization in the Kotlin build-cache metadata (build-time
			tooling). EntryStore is a Java project; kotlin-stdlib is a runtime transitive via RDF4J and
			does not exercise the build-cache path. Not reachable.
		]]></notes>
		<packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin-stdlib@.*$</packageUrl>
		<cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
	</suppress>

</suppressions>
